  "Dockerfile": 
"# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1
# Production image: docker build -t my-service .
# Installs are frozen: install the dependencies once (bun install) so that the lockfile exists.

FROM oven/bun:1 AS base
WORKDIR /app

# --- production dependencies only, at the versions of the lockfile ----------------------------------
FROM base AS deps
COPY package.json bun.lock ./
RUN bun install --frozen-lockfile --production --omit=peer

# --- build: every dependency, since the Znight compiler, Vite and TypeScript run here ---------------
FROM base AS build
COPY package.json bun.lock ./
RUN bun install --frozen-lockfile
COPY . .
# generates the DI container (src/.znight), fails on any wiring error, bundles dist/main.js
RUN bun run build

# --- runtime: the bundle and the production dependencies, as a non-root user ----------------------
FROM oven/bun:1-slim
WORKDIR /app
ENV NODE_ENV=production
COPY --from=build /app/package.json ./
COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY --from=build /app/dist ./dist
USER bun
EXPOSE 3000
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=5s --start-period=10s --retries=3 \\
  CMD ["bun", "-e", "fetch('http://127.0.0.1:' + (process.env.PORT || 3000) + '/health').then(r => process.exit(r.ok ? 0 : 1), () => process.exit(1))"]
# exec form: the runtime is PID 1 and receives SIGTERM directly (graceful shutdown)
# --no-env-file: Bun would load .env files into process.env by itself, with its own precedence
CMD ["bun", "--no-env-file", "dist/main.js"]
"
,
  "README.md": 
"# my-service

A [Znight](https://github.com/znight-org/znight) application: dependency injection resolved at **build
time** — no \`reflect-metadata\`, errors reported by the compiler with their location.

- **HTTP** with \`@znight/http\` (fastify adapter)
- **Configuration** with \`@znight/config\` (\`src/app/app.config.ts\`, \`.env\` files)
- **Observability** with \`@znight/observability\` (structured logs: pretty-printed by \`pino-pretty\` in development, JSON in production; metrics and tracing are off in \`src/app.ts\`)
- **Messaging** with \`@znight/messaging\` (in-memory broker in \`src/app.ts\`)

## Scripts

| Command | Description |
| --- | --- |
| \`bun run dev\` | Build in watch mode and restart the application on every change |
| \`bun run build\` | Production build (\`dist/main.js\`) |
| \`bun run start\` | Run the production build |
| \`bun run test\` | Run the tests |
| \`bun run typecheck\` | Generate the container, then type-check with \`tsc\` |
| \`bun run generate\` | Generate \`src/.znight/container.generated.ts\` (\`znight generate --check\` in CI) |

\`\`\`sh
bun run dev
curl localhost:3000/health
curl localhost:3000/greetings/Ada?excited=true
curl -X POST localhost:3000/greetings -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"name":"Grace"}'
\`\`\`

## Project structure

\`\`\`txt
src/
├─ app.ts                     # the plugins, shared by main.ts and the TestApp tests
├─ main.ts                    # createApplication({ plugins }) + start()
├─ .znight/                   # generated DI container (git-ignored)
└─ app/
   ├─ app.config.ts            # @Config: settings read from the environment
   ├─ greeting.consumer.ts     # @Consumer: handles the "greetings" queue
   ├─ greeting.controller.ts   # @Controller: /greetings routes
   ├─ greeting.schemas.ts      # Zod schemas
   ├─ greeting.service.ts      # @Injectable
   └─ health.controller.ts     # GET /health
test/                          # TestBed (unit) and TestApp (HTTP) tests
vite.config.ts                 # znight() plugin: generates the container, server build
znight.config.ts               # compiler options
Dockerfile                     # production image (multi-stage, non-root)
\`\`\`

Providers are discovered by the compiler from their decorators: there are no modules to declare.
Its options live in \`znight.config.ts\`, read by the \`znight()\` Vite plugin, the Bun preload of the tests and \`znight generate\`.
Add code with the generators:

\`\`\`sh
bunx znight g service users/user        # src/users/user.service.ts
bunx znight g controller users/user     # src/users/user.controller.ts
\`\`\`

## Configuration

\`AppConfig\` (\`src/app/app.config.ts\`) reads \`PORT\`, \`APP_GREETING\` and \`NODE_ENV\` from the environment
or from \`.env\` / \`.env.local\` files. Missing or invalid values stop the application at boot with
every problem listed.

\`bunfig.toml\` turns Bun's own \`.env\` loading off (\`env = false\`): the files are read by
\`@znight/config\`, the same way on Node.js and Bun.

## Docker

\`\`\`sh
docker build -t my-service .
docker run --rm -p 3000:3000 my-service
\`\`\`

The \`Dockerfile\` builds with every dependency (the Znight compiler runs during the build), then
ships \`dist/\` with the production dependencies only, on Bun, as a non-root user, with
\`NODE_ENV=production\` and a health check on \`GET /health\`. Installs are frozen: the lockfile of
\`bun install\` must exist.

## Tests

\`bun test\` regenerates the container first (\`bunfig.toml\` preloads \`@znight/compiler/bun\`).

## Learn more

- [Znight documentation](https://github.com/znight-org/znight#readme)
"
,
  "bunfig.toml": 
"# @znight/config loads the .env files (dotenv()), the same way on Node.js and Bun: Bun's own
# loading would put them in process.env first, with its own precedence
env = false

[test]
# Regenerates the DI container (src/.znight/container.generated.ts) before the tests run
preload = ["@znight/compiler/bun"]
"
