  "Dockerfile": 
"# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1
# Production image: docker build -t my-service .
# Installs are frozen: install the dependencies once (npm install) so that the lockfile exists.

FROM node:24-slim AS base
WORKDIR /app

# --- production dependencies only, at the versions of the lockfile ----------------------------------
FROM base AS deps
COPY package.json package-lock.json ./
RUN npm pkg delete devDependencies && npm ci --omit=dev

# --- build: every dependency, since the Znight compiler, Vite and TypeScript run here ---------------
FROM base AS build
COPY package.json package-lock.json ./
RUN npm ci
COPY . .
# generates the DI container (src/.znight), fails on any wiring error, bundles dist/main.js
RUN npm run build

# --- runtime: the bundle and the production dependencies, as a non-root user ----------------------
FROM node:24-slim
WORKDIR /app
ENV NODE_ENV=production
COPY --from=build /app/package.json ./
COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY --from=build /app/dist ./dist
USER node
EXPOSE 3000
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=5s --start-period=10s --retries=3 \\
  CMD ["node", "-e", "fetch('http://127.0.0.1:' + (process.env.PORT || 3000) + '/health').then(r => process.exit(r.ok ? 0 : 1), () => process.exit(1))"]
# exec form: the runtime is PID 1 and receives SIGTERM directly (graceful shutdown)
CMD ["node", "--enable-source-maps", "dist/main.js"]
"
,
  "README.md": 
"# my-service

A [Znight](https://github.com/znight-org/znight) application: dependency injection resolved at **build
time** — no \`reflect-metadata\`, errors reported by the compiler with their location.

- **HTTP** with \`@znight/http\` (fastify adapter)
- **Observability** with \`@znight/observability\` (structured logs: pretty-printed by \`pino-pretty\` in development, JSON in production; metrics and tracing are off in \`src/app.ts\`)
- **OpenAPI** with \`@znight/openapi\` (\`/openapi.json\`, Swagger UI API reference at \`/docs\`, options in \`src/openapi.ts\`)
- **GraphQL** with \`@znight/graphql\` (code-first: the schema is derived from \`src/app/greeting.resolver.ts\`)
- **WebSocket** with \`@znight/websocket\` (\`src/app/greeting.gateway.ts\`, on the HTTP port at \`/ws\`)

## Scripts

| Command | Description |
| --- | --- |
| \`npm run dev\` | Build in watch mode and restart the application on every change |
| \`npm run build\` | Production build (\`dist/main.js\`) |
| \`npm run start\` | Run the production build |
| \`npm run test\` | Run the tests |
| \`npm run typecheck\` | Generate the container, then type-check with \`tsc\` |
| \`npm run generate\` | Generate \`src/.znight/container.generated.ts\` (\`znight generate --check\` in CI) |
| \`npm run openapi\` | Write \`openapi.json\` (commit it; \`npm run openapi:check\` in CI) |

\`\`\`sh
npm run dev
curl localhost:3000/health
curl localhost:3000/greetings/Ada?excited=true
curl -X POST localhost:3000/greetings -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"name":"Grace"}'
curl localhost:3000/openapi.json        # the API reference is at http://localhost:3000/docs
curl localhost:3000/graphql -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"query":"{ greeting(name: \\"Ada\\") { message } }"}'
\`\`\`

## Project structure

\`\`\`txt
src/
├─ app.ts                     # the plugins, shared by main.ts and the TestApp tests
├─ main.ts                    # createApplication({ plugins }) + start()
├─ openapi.ts                 # @OpenApiDocument: title, description, version of openapi.json
├─ .znight/                   # generated DI container (git-ignored)
└─ app/
   ├─ greeting.controller.ts   # @Controller: /greetings routes
   ├─ greeting.gateway.ts      # @Gateway: the /ws WebSocket endpoint
   ├─ greeting.resolver.ts     # @Resolver: the greeting GraphQL query
   ├─ greeting.schemas.ts      # Zod schemas
   ├─ greeting.service.ts      # @Injectable
   └─ health.controller.ts     # GET /health
test/                          # TestBed (unit) and TestApp (HTTP) tests
vite.config.ts                 # znight() plugin: generates the container, server build
znight.config.ts               # compiler options
Dockerfile                     # production image (multi-stage, non-root)
\`\`\`

Providers are discovered by the compiler from their decorators: there are no modules to declare.
Its options live in \`znight.config.ts\`, read by the \`znight()\` Vite plugin (builds and Vitest) and \`znight generate\`.
Add code with the generators:

\`\`\`sh
npx znight g service users/user        # src/users/user.service.ts
npx znight g controller users/user     # src/users/user.controller.ts
\`\`\`

## Docker

\`\`\`sh
docker build -t my-service .
docker run --rm -p 3000:3000 my-service
\`\`\`

The \`Dockerfile\` builds with every dependency (the Znight compiler runs during the build), then
ships \`dist/\` with the production dependencies only, on Node.js, as a non-root user, with
\`NODE_ENV=production\` and a health check on \`GET /health\`. Installs are frozen: the lockfile of
\`npm install\` must exist.

## Tests

Vitest uses \`vite.config.ts\`, so the \`znight()\` plugin regenerates the container before the tests.

## Learn more

- [Znight documentation](https://github.com/znight-org/znight#readme)
"
,
